The ProvablyAI verifiable data agent kit is an open-source project under active development. To leverage it for your needs, follow these steps:

### Installation

First, install the required dependencies using npm or yarn.

```bash
# Using npm (preferred method)
npm install provably-verification-agentkit

# Alternatively, with yarn
yarn add provably-verification-agentkit
```

### Setup

Once installed, configure the agent kit for your specific use case. This typically involves setting up a verifiable data source (e.g., a blockchain or a decentralized storage platform) and defining rules to validate the data.

```javascript
// Example setup in Node.js
const VerifiableDataAgentKit = require('provably-verification-agentkit');
const agentKit = new VerifiableDataAgentKit({
  // Config options here, e.g.,
  source: 'https://your-verified-data-source.com', // URL to your verifiable data source
  rules: [
    { // Rule definition
      name: 'User Age Greater Than 18',
      validatorFunction: (data) => {
        const age = parseInt(data.age);
        return age >= 18;
      },
      description: "Ensures user is of legal age.",
    }
  ],
});

// Usage example:
agentKit.validate({
  // Data to validate
  name: 'John Doe',
  age: '30', // Converted from string to integer for validation purposes
});
```

### Validation

Use the agent kit's validation functions to check data against your defined rules. This ensures that the data is consistent and trustworthy.

```javascript
// Validate user data against a rule.
const result = agentKit.validate({
  name: 'John Doe',
  age: '30', // Converted from string to integer for validation purposes
});

// Check if the data passes the validation rules.
if (result.valid) {
  console.log('Data is valid.');
} else {
  console.error('Data failed validation.');
}
```

### Deployment

To make the agent kit operational in your application, consider deploying it as a server or using it within an existing infrastructure. This could involve setting up APIs for data validation and integration with other systems.

Remember to test the agent kit thoroughly before deployment to ensure its reliability and effectiveness.

If you have any specific questions about how to use the agent kit or need further guidance on integrating it into your project, feel free to ask!

